      "content": {
        "id": "760-001",
        "title": "Measure native custody read amplification and define the exact guarded repair",
        "description": "MASTER3178 / parent120, approved remaining D work. Produce actionable regression evidence for repeated native root/parent/handle traversal. This is a test-and-evidence preparatory task, NOT production implementation or closure. Extend the existing FakeNative test fixture with operation counters and add meaningful coverage comparing repeated reads at different directory depths. Assert existing security properties (unsafe parent rejection, identity/replacement rejection, read-only privacy behavior and handle release), without asserting an invented optimized bound. Report observed native operation counts from actually executed tests. Inspect the real producer/consumer path and identify precisely which calls can be removed or safely scoped, what identity and final reread fences must remain, and the exact production files and verification adapter required for a subsequent runtime repair. Existing host proof registry currently has no native-history profile; explain the proper closure binding without borrowing unrelated profile identities. R10 candidate failed the real 10s history budget; R11 removed read-time fchmod but did not establish performance closure. Do not repeat the full real history scan or access real custody. Preserve all existing tests and dirty baseline changes. Do not write production source, native binding, harness, config, DIRECTIVES, runtime, auth, other reports, or global memory. No build, commit, push, cleanup, start, subagents or provider fallback. Use only isolated test fixtures; complete your own injected host-bound task/result protocol with honest typed evidence. The task result notes must include UTC, path:line/hash, actual test command/exit/counts, precise repair recommendation and platform/tenant boundaries. Test-green is not product DONE.\n### goNogo\n- goCriteria: Scoped regression tests execute successfully and the task result records actual operation counts and exit code.; Native identity privacy and cleanup assertions remain intact without production code changes.; The next runtime repair and missing host-proof profile have exact file and security boundaries.; Only the declared test changes\\; no fabricated latency provider or closure evidence.\n- nogo: Missing measurements or weakened security assertions.; Production source or live runtime writes outside the task scope.\n\nBoundary clarification: write only the existing declared test file. All requested prose and actual operation counts belong in your own normal host-bound result notes, not a docs file. The supervisor creates the evidence report. Do not create a report elsewhere.",
        "model": "gpt-5.6-sol",
        "effort": "high",
        "priority": "NORMAL",
        "reason": "Directive (model: gpt-5.6-sol -- resolved from scope/complexity/plan)",
        "scope": {
